# Hooks in .claude/settings.json run code on EVERY member's machine on every tool call, so anyone who can merge here
# can run code on the whole team's machines. Treat these paths like a build script: required review, named owners.
# Replace @your-org/agent-maintainers with real owners, and enable "Require review from Code Owners" on main.

/.claude/                @your-org/agent-maintainers
/tools/                  @your-org/agent-maintainers
/insight/                @your-org/agent-maintainers
/agents-src/             @your-org/agent-maintainers
/agent/                  @your-org/agent-maintainers
/CLAUDE.md               @your-org/agent-maintainers

# memory/ is the team's shared knowledge: any member may propose, one other member approves.
# Every memory's description lands in EVERY member's session context, so read memory diffs as you would read code:
# a line that tells the agent to run, fetch or ignore something is an attack, not a note.
/memory/                 @your-org/team
# Lessons reach further - their trigger is in every session AND compiled into the role agents' system prompts -
# so they need a maintainer, like the code. (Later rules win in CODEOWNERS.)
/memory/lessons/         @your-org/agent-maintainers
